## 4. Worker rules

1. Write only the assigned lane; do not modify root GOAL or another Worker's records.
2. After user authorization, read the assigned package/code and establish `READY_REVIEW` from the inherited Reviewer or `SELF_REVIEW_READY` for explicit self-review.
3. Only then create an active Goal referencing this file's absolute path and start execution; report any configuration mismatch instead of silently falling back.
4. For each completed item, update execution, mark `implemented_pending_review`, and invoke the configured review mode.
5. Mark `approved` only after an explicit `REVIEW` or `SELF` receipt.
6. Notify the Orchestrator about cross-lane issues, shared hotspots, pauses, or integration needs.

## 5. Completion conditions

- [ ] Every assigned item is `approved`.
- [ ] The lane-level integrated audit passes.
- [ ] Exact commit or artifact is recorded and the worktree is clean.
- [ ] The Orchestrator has been notified that integration may begin.
